// Title: Permanent WMI Event Subscription Created from the Command Line
// ATT&CK: T1546.003 | Tactic: PrivilegeEscalation, Persistence | Sigma id: 3c9eed57-ad3c-4116-8872-baf2c60d4d92
// Data source: DeviceProcessEvents (Microsoft Defender for Endpoint / Defender XDR connector)
// Severity: High
// False positives: Management agents that register WMI subscriptions (SCCM, some monitoring tools)
// Suggested analytics rule: run every 15m, look back 30m, alert when results > 0.
// Entity mapping: Host = DeviceName, Account = AccountName, Process = ProcessCommandLine
// The time filter below is for ad-hoc hunting; the analytics rule's lookback applies when scheduled.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1d)
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "__EventFilter" or ProcessCommandLine contains "CommandLineEventConsumer" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ActiveScriptEventConsumer" or ProcessCommandLine contains "__FilterToConsumerBinding"
| project TimeGenerated, DeviceName, AccountName, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine, FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine
